  "title": "Despite being a Switch 2 exclusive, The Duskbloods closed network test had more applications than Elden Ring Nightreign",
  "content": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/The-Duskbloods-%E2%80%93-Nintendo-Direct-_-Nintendo-Switch-2-1-46-screenshot.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp\" /> <p>The Duskbloods is already looking like it's going to be a very popular game. Developer FromSoftware revealed <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-check-network-test-access\">the game's network test, which finished yesterday</a>, attracted more player applications than those for <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/elden-ring-nightreign\">Elden Ring Nightreign</a>, despite it only being available for one platform: <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/platforms/switch-2\">Switch 2</a>.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-closed-network-test-more-applications-nightreign\">Read more</a></p>",
